cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this model, please cite it as below, and cite hae and the datasets (see NOTICE.md)."
title: "hae-n-ir-ext-kdf: a real-time thermal person detector for search-and-rescue drones"
type: software
authors:
  - name: "The hae authors"
version: 1.0.0
date-released: 2026-10-15
license: MIT
repository-code: "https://github.com/sashapiscivca-svg/hae-n-ir-ext-kdf"
url: "https://huggingface.co/alexshynkarenk0/hae-n-ir-ext-kdf"
keywords:
  - search and rescue
  - object detection
  - thermal imaging
  - drones
  - real-time
  - knowledge distillation
  - Raspberry Pi
abstract: >-
  hae-n-ir-ext-kdf is a 54 k-parameter person detector for thermal (LWIR) aerial imagery, the real-time member of the hae family,
  trained from scratch on openly licensed civilian datasets with knowledge distillation from a larger hae model, and fast enough
  for live video on a Raspberry Pi Zero 2 W.
references:
